  "body": "In CustomElements v0 you could use the `.name` field to get the defined tag name, but CustomElements v1 does not offer such a field. `localName` can be used within an instance but this prohibits use in, for example, static methods.\n\nThis was discussed in the WCCG F2F, tracked in\nhttps://github.com/WICG/webcomponents/issues/566. The conclusion of the F2F was to write up a spec change and WPT tests.\n\n<!--\nThank you for contributing to the HTML Standard! Please describe the change you are making and complete the checklist below if your change is not editorial.\n-->\n\n- [x] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * WebKit (https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/pull/13053)\n   * Chromium (https://chromestatus.com/feature/5199783177748480)\n   * Mozilla (https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/785)\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/39640\n- [x] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chromium: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=1435389\n   * Gecko: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1829335\n   * WebKit: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=255778\n   * ~~Deno (only for timers, structured clone, base64 utils, channel messaging, module resolution, web workers, and web storage): …~~\n   * ~~Node.js (only for timers, structured clone, base64 utils, channel messaging, and module resolution): …~~\n- [x] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed:\n  - [x] [MDN docs](https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/27465)\n  - [x] [MDN data](https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/20186)\n\n(See [WHATWG Working Mode: Changes](https://whatwg.org/working-mode#changes) for more details.)\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is